WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.330
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Wednesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.060
Today's about going public: Anthropic's stock

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.180
market debut could value it at $1.4 trillion.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.300
And the founders' stated aim? To "bring forth an age of miracles."

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.740
The same day, Claude got its own office tools: spreadsheets,

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.020
whiteboards, dashboards. Microsoft's stock dipped.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.860
Google released Gemini 4 Carbon, its strongest model.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.560
One prompt can spin up a team of agents.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.670
And ChatGPT now lets businesses claim verified profiles,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.870
with their own agents to answer your questions.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.520
Over at Google DeepMind,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.840
AI agents helped prove that Signal's encryption works as intended.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.130
Now, the money.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:06.470
Chip giant TSMC is putting up to $1 billion into Anthropic and OpenAI.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.430
Alibaba's chip design unit, T-Head, filed to go public too, in Hong Kong.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.910
Mercor, which uses human experts to train AI, is now valued at $20 billion.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.640
Oura, the smart ring company, is buying an AI doctor startup for $625 million.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.120
A recent MIT grad used Anthropic's new model to

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.240
crack an 18-year-old quantum computing puzzle.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.850
He told TechCrunch, "this might be the last paper I ever put out."

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.350
The catch? After a rogue OpenAI agent's breach,

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.550
Australia's creating an AI safety regulator.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.670
And Qantas is cutting 850 jobs in an AI overhaul.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.920
Humanoids running Google's new robot AI pac

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.970
ked car parts at Mercedes with 96% success.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.610
Amazon's Ring unveiled a drone that flies room to room inside your home,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.780
checking on things.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.690
In Antarctica, a humanoid robot entered an ultramarathon.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:22.430
Its battery died after 3 kilometers.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.450
Going public means letting everyone see you stumble.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.500
It's also how you earn their trust.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
